{
  "title": "How Did Ancient Humans Actually Sleep?",
  "language": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "chapter": "The Night",
      "frame": "scene",
      "bg": "deep_night",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "prop",
          "name": "moon",
          "x": 0.85,
          "y": 0.17,
          "scale": 0.9
        },
        {
          "type": "prop",
          "name": "campfire",
          "id": "fire",
          "x": 0.5,
          "scale": 1.1
        },
        {
          "type": "character",
          "id": "me",
          "variant": "you_main",
          "pose": "sleeping",
          "x": 0.22
        },
        {
          "type": "character",
          "id": "elder",
          "variant": "ancient_human",
          "pose": "sitting",
          "attach": {
            "to": "fire",
            "side": "right",
            "gap": 60
          }
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You wake up in the middle of the night."
        },
        {
          "text": "No alarm. No phone. Just the crackle of a fire.",
          "change": {
            "me": {
              "pose": "sitting",
              "x": 0.3,
              "expression": "surprise"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "And you are not the only one awake.",
          "change": {
            "elder": {
              "expression": "happy"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "frame": "concept_text",
      "text": "300,000 YEARS",
      "sub": "of sleeping without a clock",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "For roughly three hundred thousand years, this was completely normal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chapter": "The Eight-Hour Myth",
      "frame": "scene",
      "bg": "neutral_modern",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "prop",
          "name": "bed",
          "id": "bed",
          "x": 0.5,
          "scale": 1.3
        },
        {
          "type": "character",
          "variant": "modern_neutral",
          "pose": "sleeping",
          "x": 0.5,
          "y": 0.72,
          "extras": [
            "zzz"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "label",
          "text": "8 HOURS STRAIGHT",
          "y": 0.15
        },
        {
          "type": "red_x",
          "id": "x"
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Today you are told to sleep eight hours in one solid block."
        },
        {
          "text": "But historian Roger Ekirch found that this idea is surprisingly new.",
          "show": [
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "frame": "scene",
      "bg": "ancient_savanna",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "prop",
          "name": "acacia",
          "x": 0.8
        },
        {
          "type": "character",
          "id": "thinker",
          "variant": "archaeologist",
          "pose": "thinking",
          "expression": "thinking",
          "x": 0.32
        },
        {
          "type": "thought",
          "id": "bubble",
          "of": "thinker",
          "prop": "book"
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Ekirch spent years reading diaries, court records and old medical books."
        },
        {
          "text": "Again and again, people wrote about a first sleep and a second sleep.",
          "show": [
            "bubble"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chapter": "Two Sleeps",
      "frame": "split",
      "left": {
        "bg": "deep_night",
        "title": "FIRST SLEEP",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "character",
            "variant": "ancient_human",
            "pose": "sleeping",
            "x": 0.5,
            "extras": [
              "zzz"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "bg": "calm_night",
        "title": "SECOND SLEEP",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "prop",
            "name": "campfire",
            "id": "f2",
            "x": 0.35
          },
          {
            "type": "character",
            "variant": "ancient_human",
            "pose": "sitting",
            "expression": "happy",
            "attach": {
              "to": "f2",
              "side": "right",
              "gap": 40
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You would fall asleep a few hours after dark."
        },
        {
          "text": "Then wake around midnight for an hour or two, talk, tend the fire, and sleep again."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chapter": "The Evidence",
      "frame": "stats",
      "title": "HOURS OF SLEEP PER NIGHT",
      "bars": [
        {
          "label": "Hunter-gatherers (shortest)",
          "value": 5.7,
          "display": "5.7 h"
        },
        {
          "label": "Hunter-gatherers (longest)",
          "value": 7.1,
          "display": "7.1 h"
        },
        {
          "label": "Recommended",
          "value": 8,
          "display": "8 h",
          "color": "red"
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "In 2015, Jerome Siegel measured sleep in three hunter gatherer groups."
        },
        {
          "text": "The Hadza, the San and the Tsimane slept between five point seven and seven point one hours. Less than you are told you need."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "frame": "timeline",
      "title": "WHEN DID SLEEP CHANGE?",
      "highlight": 2,
      "events": [
        {
          "label": "PREHISTORY",
          "text": "Fire and darkness",
          "icon": "campfire"
        },
        {
          "label": "1600s",
          "text": "Two sleeps",
          "icon": "lantern"
        },
        {
          "label": "1880s",
          "text": "Electric light",
          "icon": "lightbulb"
        },
        {
          "label": "TODAY",
          "text": "Screens at midnight",
          "icon": "phone"
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "So what changed? Light."
        },
        {
          "text": "Once cheap artificial light arrived, the quiet hour in the middle of the night slowly disappeared."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chapter": "Back to You",
      "frame": "scene",
      "bg": "neutral_modern",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "prop",
          "name": "clock",
          "x": 0.8,
          "y": 0.3,
          "scale": 0.8
        },
        {
          "type": "character",
          "id": "me",
          "variant": "you_main",
          "pose": "holding",
          "holding": "phone",
          "expression": "worry_sadness",
          "x": 0.4,
          "extras": [
            "sweat"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "thought",
          "id": "q",
          "of": "me",
          "text": "3 AM?!"
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "So the next time you wake up at three in the morning and panic,",
          "show": [
            "q"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "remember that your ancestors did exactly the same thing.",
          "change": {
            "me": {
              "expression": "calm_content",
              "extras": []
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "You wake up in the middle of the night. And that might be the most human thing about you.",
          "change": {
            "me": {
              "expression": "happy"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
